{"title": "My $15 USB-C Hub is a Game Changer for My Dorm Setup", "body": "Okay, so I've been trying to keep my desk setup as minimal and cheap as possible since I'm a college student, and honestly, I'm not into blowing my budget on fancy gear. I was looking for something that would just make my life slightly less annoying, and I stumbled upon this super basic USB-C hub for like fifteen bucks. It’s just a little block with a bunch of ports—HDMI, USB-A, and a USB-C charging port. 

At first, I thought, 'Great, another piece of junk.' But I hooked it up to my old, clunky laptop, and it was surprisingly useful. I can now plug my external monitor, my mouse, and my phone charger all into one single port. Before, I had to use three separate dongles and adapters, and it was a total mess of cables everywhere. 

It’s not the fastest thing on the market, and the build quality feels pretty basic, but for the price, it’s seriously amazing. It has completely decluttered my desk space and made connecting peripherals way easier. If you’re trying to set up a basic multi-device station without spending a fortune, I highly recommend checking out these budget hubs. Anyone else found a hidden gem like this?"}

